                <pb facs="0359" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.51/286: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-23T17:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 24,
                            3.34 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>National Legislative Assembly yesterday passed bill authorizing each bank to set
                    aside 10,000,000 pesos of a new issue for a fund to be used in agricultural and
                    building loans at 4 per cent. It now awaits presidential approval which will be
                    given as the measure is of his own making. This means sixty millions additional
                    in controvertible [<hi rendition="#italic">convertible</hi>] paper.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
